    "name": "connect_repairs_a_pid_weight_above_one",
    "description": "The owner's controller (holey 51.27, PCB v1.1) after an earlier Rust build wrote $24=1.000000 and $32=1.000000: readFloat stored 1.00000011 (printed 1.00000011), above the 1 PID::SetTunings accepts, so the L, R and Z position PIDs kept zero gains and no motor moved (2026-11-15). The rest of $$ is the owner's real report (recording 20261114-014854). The values compare equal to webcontrol.json's 1 at the printed precision, but the firmware refuses them, so WebControl rewrites both as $24=1 and $32=1 (an integer reads exactly), with $13 once, then reads $$ back (spec/firmware.md §4, B2).",
